    "step8_outcome_verification": {
      "primary_intent": "Extract and report specific labeled fields from the Unicode Unihan record for code point U+4E00—glyph, decimal/UTF-8/UTF-16 encodings, total strokes, definition, and the four language readings—copied exactly as displayed from that record (no outside knowledge or self-transliteration). A reasonable user would be flexible on formatting/bullets, but not on missing fields or any value that isn’t demonstrably taken from the Unihan record.",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor formatting choices (bullets, ordering) are not important as long as the correct values are provided.\n\nCritical issues: The agent’s output includes a definition and four language readings (kDefinition, kMandarin, kJapaneseOn, kKorean, kVietnamese), but the provided DOM-model evidence for the session does not show any of those labeled fields/values anywhere—only the header identifying “Unihan data for U+4E00,” the Glyph line (一), the Encoding Forms table (Decimal 19968, UTF-8 E4 B8 80, UTF-16 4E00), and kTotalStrokes = 1. Because the task explicitly requires using only the supplied Unihan record and copying the labeled fields exactly as displayed, reporting values that are not evidenced in the record view we can verify is effectively unsupported and risks being fabricated or sourced externally. This is not a minor omission; definition and the four readings are key requested deliverables.\n\nWhat the agent did accomplish: It successfully accessed the correct Unihan page for U+4E00 and correctly reported the code point, displayed glyph, decimal value, UTF-8, UTF-16, and total stroke count—these are all explicitly confirmed by the DOM-model snapshots.\n\nOverall outcome: The agent did not reliably complete the primary intent because it failed the core requirement to extract (and thus provide verifiable, record-derived) definition and all four language readings from the supplied record. From an average user perspective, receiving potentially untrustworthy values for half of the requested fields means the task is not successfully completed.",
      "output_success": false
    },
